1
00:01:50,740 --> 00:01:53,480
Wow...

2
00:01:53,900 --> 00:01:58,020
The rumors don't do it justice.

3
00:01:58,950 --> 00:02:03,180
Iceland is a harsh land.

4
00:02:04,450 --> 00:02:07,100
There are no trees at all.

5
00:02:09,890 --> 00:02:13,250
The sun's so low in the sky.

6
00:02:14,300 --> 00:02:17,860
I get it now. A land without farms, huh?

7
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:22,110
You can't grow anything
when the days are so short.

8
00:02:22,830 --> 00:02:24,600
It's winter, after all.

9
00:02:25,790 --> 00:02:29,230
During the summer, the days are long.

10
00:02:29,750 --> 00:02:34,650
Some people grow wheat
where conditions are better,

11
00:02:34,650 --> 00:02:38,610
but it's not nearly enough to fill the
stomachs of the island-dwellers.

12
00:02:39,080 --> 00:02:43,470
Are all the island-dwellers
shepherds and ranchers, then?

13
00:02:43,870 --> 00:02:46,930
No, there are craftsmen and fishermen, too.

14
00:02:48,570 --> 00:02:54,410
There isn't enough pastureland
for everyone to raise livestock,

15
00:02:54,410 --> 00:02:58,370
so some people live
together and fish instead.

16
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:03,200
Thorfinn's village is one of those.

17
00:03:04,460 --> 00:03:05,820
Huh.

18
00:03:06,220 --> 00:03:09,900
What does that mean? Didn't you live here?

19
00:03:10,430 --> 00:03:14,310
But I was just a child.

20
00:03:15,690 --> 00:03:18,100
I left home when I was
around six years old.

21
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:24,180
Since then, it's been
a good... uh, at least...

22
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:28,050
Wait, how old am I?

23
00:03:29,410 --> 00:03:33,580
Thorfinn, Einar,
the village is coming into view.

24
00:03:38,190 --> 00:03:39,450
Whoa...

25
00:03:39,450 --> 00:03:42,670
I suddenly feel scared.

26
00:03:42,670 --> 00:03:45,920
How am I supposed to
face my mother and sister?

27
00:03:48,990 --> 00:03:52,590
You'd better prepare for the worst,
my "prodigal son."

28
00:03:54,750 --> 00:03:57,860
You're finally returning home.

29
00:03:55,020 --> 00:04:01,030
Home.

30
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:08,240
Okay, that's it.

31
00:04:09,870 --> 00:04:11,370
Good.

32
00:04:25,590 --> 00:04:26,630
There!

33
00:04:32,350 --> 00:04:33,580
Thorfinn...

34
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:39,500
The villagers are waiting for you.

35
00:04:51,420 --> 00:04:52,200
Who's he?

36
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:53,650
No idea.

37
00:04:53,650 --> 00:04:55,960
Did Ylva have a little brother?

38
00:04:59,450 --> 00:05:01,860
What's my name, then?

39
00:05:01,860 --> 00:05:02,560
What?

40
00:05:02,960 --> 00:05:06,220
If you used to live here,
then you should know.

41
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:11,970
F... Faxi?

42
00:05:12,280 --> 00:05:13,400
He got it wrong.

43
00:05:13,400 --> 00:05:14,900
He's suspicious.

44
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:16,440
Should we tie him up?

45
00:05:16,440 --> 00:05:20,480
No, wait. I can't help it. It's been years.

46
00:05:21,710 --> 00:05:23,220
Mister Leif...

47
00:05:25,850 --> 00:05:29,110
Fine. I guess we'll let him see Ylva.

48
00:05:29,110 --> 00:05:30,990
Yeah.

49
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:36,540
Ylva's over there, arguing
with the Norwegian merchant.

50
00:05:38,850 --> 00:05:44,880
I warned you not to be
so greedy here, Berge.

51
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:50,760
S-Sorry, Ylva. I w-won't do it again.

52
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:54,290
Huh? What was that? I didn't hear you.

53
00:05:54,290 --> 00:05:59,570
Th-That's enough, Ylva.
He returned our money.

54
00:05:59,570 --> 00:06:01,920
Hey, Ylva.

55
00:06:04,860 --> 00:06:08,650
I finally brought him back.

56
00:06:09,870 --> 00:06:11,250
This is Thorfinn.

57
00:06:20,300 --> 00:06:22,300
Thorfinn...

58
00:06:24,880 --> 00:06:26,160
Thorfinn.

59
00:06:29,740 --> 00:06:31,010
Sister.

60
00:06:34,670 --> 00:06:35,720
Sister!

61
00:06:39,710 --> 00:06:42,620
I don't know a Thorfinn!

62
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:47,760
Come on, Ylva.
It's your little brother, Thorfinn.

63
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:49,400
Little brother?

64
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:53,600
Come to think of it,
that might've been his name.

65
00:06:53,600 --> 00:06:56,370
My little brother died when he was a kid.

66
00:06:56,370 --> 00:06:58,640
He's actually alive.

67
00:06:58,640 --> 00:07:01,680
I told you I met him in York before.

68
00:07:01,680 --> 00:07:05,120
Then why didn't you bring him back then?

69
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:08,460
Well, you know, there was a lot going on...

70
00:07:11,690 --> 00:07:16,100
You made that story up to cheer up
my mother and me, didn't you?

71
00:07:16,960 --> 00:07:18,800
Thank you, Mister Leif.

72
00:07:19,740 --> 00:07:22,480
No, actually...

73
00:07:22,870 --> 00:07:25,060
More importantly...

74
00:07:25,060 --> 00:07:26,360
Huh?

75
00:07:26,980 --> 00:07:32,360
Hey, shorty. You've got some balls
to trick Mister Leif like this.

76
00:07:32,360 --> 00:07:33,360
No, wait!

77
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:35,920
If you've got something
to say, spit it out.

78
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:39,140
Man, this has gotten really complicated.

79
00:07:40,140 --> 00:07:44,940
It's surprisingly difficult
to prove who you are.

80
00:07:54,310 --> 00:07:56,870
Let's go to your home, Thorfinn.

81
00:07:56,870 --> 00:07:59,640
Helga will know who you are.

82
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:02,130
Thorfinn...

83
00:08:02,130 --> 00:08:03,360
Who's that?

84
00:08:03,360 --> 00:08:04,980
He's taking this hard.

85
00:08:07,610 --> 00:08:09,300
I can't blame them.

86
00:08:09,810 --> 00:08:14,200
I'd nearly forgotten the faces
of my sister and mother, too.

87
00:08:16,720 --> 00:08:19,390
It's no surprise they've forgotten me.

88
00:08:23,260 --> 00:08:26,540
Who cares if they have?

89
00:08:27,370 --> 00:08:31,890
You get to see your mother's face
after wandering for over a decade.

90
00:08:31,890 --> 00:08:34,830
If you don't consider yourself lucky,
the gods will smite you.

91
00:08:36,140 --> 00:08:39,240
I was separated from my parents as a kid.

92
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:42,060
I don't even know where they are now.

93
00:08:43,050 --> 00:08:45,930
I'm jealous of you.

94
00:08:49,450 --> 00:08:53,200
Or shall I go play the devoted son for you?

95
00:08:55,610 --> 00:08:58,080
No. I'm sorry, Bug-Eyes.

96
00:08:58,630 --> 00:08:59,730
Thank you.

97
00:09:17,780 --> 00:09:20,340
Grandma, who's Thorfinn?

98
00:09:20,340 --> 00:09:21,470
Tor-fin...

99
00:09:29,020 --> 00:09:30,240
Thorfinn...

100
00:09:31,560 --> 00:09:32,500
Ma!

101
00:09:32,500 --> 00:09:33,860
What are you doing?

102
00:09:33,860 --> 00:09:36,340
Stop making things more complicated.

103
00:09:36,340 --> 00:09:38,480
Aw, c'mon. Who cares?

104
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:42,050
No, Helga. This one is...

105
00:09:47,840 --> 00:09:49,470
Thorfinn...

106
00:09:52,380 --> 00:09:53,780
Mother...

107
00:09:56,430 --> 00:10:01,010
You've grown so much.

108
00:10:08,540 --> 00:10:10,750
You look just like him.

109
00:10:12,570 --> 00:10:17,150
You really are your father's son.

110
00:10:28,890 --> 00:10:30,620
Mother...

111
00:10:31,710 --> 00:10:37,330
I'm sorry for everything.

112
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:44,320
Welcome home, Thorfinn.

113
00:11:18,730 --> 00:11:21,880
Mother, I heard Thorfinn's back.

114
00:11:22,210 --> 00:11:24,400
Welcome back, Dad.

115
00:11:24,400 --> 00:11:25,840
Welcome back.

116
00:11:28,640 --> 00:11:29,950
Thorfinn...

117
00:11:37,820 --> 00:11:39,150
Ari...

118
00:11:40,860 --> 00:11:42,030
Thorfinn.

119
00:11:46,170 --> 00:11:48,850
Thorfinn, I'm sorry.

120
00:11:50,270 --> 00:11:53,920
Because of us, Mister Thors...

121
00:12:03,150 --> 00:12:07,340
Ari, I was an idiot.

122
00:12:17,080 --> 00:12:18,560
Well, then...

123
00:12:22,330 --> 00:12:25,070
Where are you going, Mister Einar?

124
00:12:25,360 --> 00:12:28,570
I should be leaving for the night.

125
00:12:28,970 --> 00:12:33,620
Mister Leif's crew is staying at
the gothi's house. I'll join them there.

126
00:12:34,470 --> 00:12:37,200
You should stay here.

127
00:12:37,200 --> 00:12:40,930
It's a bit cramped,
but we'll figure it out.

128
00:12:41,470 --> 00:12:43,130
But...

129
00:12:43,760 --> 00:12:48,940
If you're Thorfinn's brother,
that makes you my son.

130
00:12:44,040 --> 00:12:45,560
This is my eldest son.

131
00:12:45,560 --> 00:12:47,310
Nice to meet you.

132
00:12:47,310 --> 00:12:48,940
Hello.

133
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:54,690
This is your home. Don't be shy.

134
00:13:01,270 --> 00:13:07,740
Listen to this, Mother. That stingy
merchant raised the price of salt again.

135
00:13:08,780 --> 00:13:12,920
Hey, it's you again!
How dare you come into our home?

136
00:13:12,920 --> 00:13:15,760
Oh, uh... excuse the intrusion?

137
00:13:15,760 --> 00:13:17,620
Ylva, you haven't heard the—.

138
00:13:17,620 --> 00:13:19,730
Is this an inheritance scam, huh?

139
00:13:19,260 --> 00:13:19,910
What?

140
00:13:19,730 --> 00:13:23,170
Go find a rich family to trick.

141
00:13:19,910 --> 00:13:21,620
Ma's so fast.

142
00:13:21,620 --> 00:13:23,170
And strong.

143
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:25,720
Ylva, wait.

144
00:13:25,720 --> 00:13:26,420
Huh?

145
00:13:27,100 --> 00:13:31,440
It's really him. Thorfinn's
really come home.

146
00:13:31,440 --> 00:13:33,120
It's really him?

147
00:13:33,810 --> 00:13:37,250
What? I-It can't be.

148
00:13:37,250 --> 00:13:40,960
No way. Mister Leif didn't make it up?

149
00:13:43,230 --> 00:13:45,280
What? Really?

150
00:13:48,630 --> 00:13:51,330
He's the real Thorfinn?

151
00:13:52,780 --> 00:13:55,090
I'm home, Sister.

152
00:13:59,920 --> 00:14:01,170
Thorfinn...

153
00:14:01,170 --> 00:14:02,340
Sister!

154
00:14:04,440 --> 00:14:08,400
Where have you been until now?

155
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:25,110
Hey... Are you okay, Thorfinn?

156
00:14:26,780 --> 00:14:29,870
I'm fine, Einar.

157
00:14:30,570 --> 00:14:34,240
I'm used to getting hit.

158
00:14:43,010 --> 00:14:43,740
That...

159
00:14:44,670 --> 00:14:46,800
That was just one hit...

160
00:14:50,230 --> 00:14:52,360
Ma's so strong.

161
00:14:52,360 --> 00:14:54,470
You're amazing, Ma.

162
00:14:54,470 --> 00:14:57,220
Ma's the strongest.

163
00:15:46,170 --> 00:15:47,340
That night,

164
00:15:48,580 --> 00:15:56,740
Thorfinn told his family about everything
he'd experienced over the past 16 years.

165
00:16:00,010 --> 00:16:04,920
From Thor's death to his
departure from Ketil's farm.

166
00:16:10,840 --> 00:16:15,760
Though he spoke matter-of-factly
and covered only the key points,

167
00:16:15,760 --> 00:16:18,390
his story of hatred and strife,

168
00:16:20,590 --> 00:16:22,390
death and destruction,

169
00:16:25,660 --> 00:16:27,480
despair and regret,

170
00:16:30,860 --> 00:16:33,740
sadness and rebirth

171
00:16:35,240 --> 00:16:38,590
left everyone who heard
it at a loss for words.

172
00:16:48,380 --> 00:16:50,800
The people I killed,

173
00:16:52,350 --> 00:16:56,630
the slaves who died in despair...

174
00:16:58,320 --> 00:17:03,250
They might've had warm
families like this one.

175
00:17:06,890 --> 00:17:08,850
My sins are heavy.

176
00:17:11,800 --> 00:17:18,400
I have to go to Vinland
to create a peaceful land.

177
00:17:24,810 --> 00:17:26,210
Do it.

178
00:17:28,330 --> 00:17:29,660
Mother...

179
00:17:30,290 --> 00:17:36,380
There are many people who wish
they could flee from this world.

180
00:17:37,690 --> 00:17:45,520
Thors and I fled Jomsborg, the land
of warriors, and came to this island.

181
00:17:47,950 --> 00:17:57,950
For those fleeing from war and slavery,
far beyond the horizon,

182
00:17:59,480 --> 00:18:05,980
you will build a peaceful land where
you'll wait to welcome those people there.

183
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:16,750
You must live to do that,
Thorfinn, son of Thors.

184
00:18:21,420 --> 00:18:23,790
Thank you, Mother.

185
00:18:26,910 --> 00:18:31,670
So basically, you're going to
establish a country in Vinland?

186
00:18:31,670 --> 00:18:33,770
Sounds like a large-scale endeavor.

187
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:36,830
He's right.

188
00:18:37,830 --> 00:18:40,370
I can tell you're determined.

189
00:18:40,800 --> 00:18:43,700
But you'll need people,
livestock, materials...

190
00:18:44,150 --> 00:18:46,560
You'll need to buy more boats, too.

191
00:18:47,490 --> 00:18:49,200
It all comes down to money.

192
00:18:49,610 --> 00:18:54,510
It won't be easy pulling together
that much money.

193
00:19:00,010 --> 00:19:03,170
Without my help, that is.

194
00:19:06,640 --> 00:19:09,010
Thank you, Mister Leif.

195
00:19:09,560 --> 00:19:12,120
You're not quitting sailing yet?

196
00:19:12,120 --> 00:19:13,690
I figured you'd say that, Mister Leif.

197
00:19:13,690 --> 00:19:15,800
Will it really be that easy?

198
00:19:15,800 --> 00:19:17,190
They'll be fine.

199
00:19:17,190 --> 00:19:20,070
Don't worry. There are
plenty of ways to do it.

200
00:19:20,070 --> 00:19:23,320
Don't push yourself too hard, Dad.

201
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:28,110
I'm not pushing myself. You still
don't understand the kind of man I am.

202
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:53,730
I can't believe you actually went with him.

203
00:19:54,940 --> 00:19:56,220
Sister...

204
00:20:00,750 --> 00:20:01,740
I'm sorry.

205
00:20:08,720 --> 00:20:12,860
Our father was a truly amazing man.

206
00:20:13,980 --> 00:20:16,820
He was strong and kind.

207
00:20:17,900 --> 00:20:22,880
He was looking far ahead
at something I couldn't see.

208
00:20:30,560 --> 00:20:33,580
Well, he was a strange man.

209
00:20:57,730 --> 00:20:59,540
Whose grave is that?

210
00:21:00,620 --> 00:21:04,460
Someone Father once tried to protect.

211
00:21:06,410 --> 00:21:09,510
Were they important?

212
00:21:10,860 --> 00:21:12,350
He was a slave.

213
00:21:13,260 --> 00:21:15,810
He ran away from his master.

214
00:21:15,810 --> 00:21:19,780
My father saved him when
he lay dying on the ground.

215
00:21:20,940 --> 00:21:25,650
My father apparently
traded eight sheep for him.

216
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:28,080
Eight sheep?

217
00:21:32,190 --> 00:21:36,190
I guess you get your
good nature from your dad.

218
00:21:53,180 --> 00:21:55,750
Man, it's cold.

219
00:21:55,750 --> 00:21:58,890
It's even colder around here at night.

220
00:21:58,890 --> 00:22:01,180
I'm heading back, Thorfinn.

221
00:22:13,120 --> 00:22:14,130
Hey.

222
00:22:17,400 --> 00:22:21,540
Where do the people who
want to run away from here go?

223
00:22:28,170 --> 00:22:31,490
You already know the
answer to that, don't you?
